# File spec for ./rhai_checker.rs — the Rhai static lane of the ./ linting tree. The
# pipeline order, virtual-path feeding and exit verdict belong to ./../package/lint.sdd
# (driver — reference shapes, never restate); the finding/level model is ./mod.sdd's, the
# level-resolution + directive-PARSER contract is ./config.sdd's — THIS file owns the
# rhai/… rule semantics, the suppression lane each rule wires to, and the frozen lint-vs-
# runtime name tables. Calibration reference for style: /common/src/tools.sdd via siblings.

Spec: RhaiChecker

Platform: Rust

Purpose:
  Statically lint every Rhai source of a package — file-scanned AST rules plus cross-file
    finalize rules — without ever running a script. The engine is the stock @rhai @Engine
    (zero Vynil registrations): @Engine::compile is a pure syntax/structure scan, so no
    function name is ever resolved, no module is ever opened (imports are only
    existence-checked), and any call to any identifier parses clean. One @RhaiChecker
    instance accumulates cross-file bookkeeping (imports, entry-point defining stems,
    defined/called function names) across its per-file @check_file calls and discharges
    `rhai/unused-script` and `rhai/unused-function` in @finalize. Owns all fourteen
    `rhai/…` rule ids, their built-in levels, their message templates, and exactly which
    suppression lane (config / file-union directive / per-line directive / none) each rule
    is wired to — including the seven rules wired to no lane at all.

References:
  ./mod.sdd — @LintFinding (built here per finding: rule/level/file/line/message) and
    @LintLevel; the append-only collector contract, so this file's emission order IS the
    report order the driver sees.
  ./config.sdd — @resolve_level ladder and @parse_inline_disables map shape (1-based keys,
    the key `0` never exists); THIS spec is the truth for the cross-seam item it carries:
    which rhai rules pass which inline argument to @resolve_level and which report levels
    @resolve_level never sees.
  ./../package/lint.sdd — the only driver: builds @new with @package_dir, @config_dir,
    @script_dir.as_deref(), package and config; @check_file per scanned `.rhai` file with
    the @strip_prefix-relative @Path, then on the virtual `package.yaml#value_script` and
    the prefly virtual paths; @finalize once, findings @extend-ed last.
  /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — THE runtime engine: constructor assemblies, resolver-dir
    semantics, the `256`/`128` runtime expression depths, and the registrations the frozen
    tables below diverge from.
  /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd — @VynilPackageSource and @VynilPackageType: @usage drives
    the @new resolver subdirectory and gates `rhai/wrong-package-type`.

Depends on:
  @crate::linting — @LintConfig, @LintFinding, @LintLevel, @parse_inline_disables, bound
    through the ./mod.rs re-exports rather than the ./config.rs paths.
  @common::rhaihandler — import path only, for the re-exported @AST, @ASTNode, @Engine,
    @Expr, @ParseError, @Stmt vocabulary; NO @Script constructor or registration of that
    module is used here (the asymmetry is the subject of the name-drift tasks).
  @common::vynilpackage — @VynilPackageSource, @VynilPackageType.
  @rhai `1.20.0` requested (workspace-locked), a DIRECT agent-crate dependency used only
    for @OptimizationLevel; the engine types arrive through the @common re-export, so the
    two import paths must stay version-locked together.
  @std — @fs::read_dir and @Path::exists (list and existence only). This file NEVER reads
    script content from disk: sources arrive as @check_file arguments; @PathBuf joins,
    @HashSet/@HashMap bookkeeping, and string-table membership are its only other tools.

Exposes:
  @RhaiChecker — `pub struct RhaiChecker<'a>` with private fields @pkg, @config,
    @resolver_paths (@Vec<@PathBuf>), @entry_scripts (@HashSet<@PathBuf>),
    @imported_scripts (@HashSet<@String>), @scripts_with_entry_points (@HashSet<@String>),
    @defined_functions (@Vec of name+@PathBuf pairs, declaration order), @called_functions
    (@HashSet<@String>). Crate-only reach: the @mod linting declaration is private in
    ./../main.rs and the lib target (named `client`) does not compile it — nothing outside
    the agent binary depends on this surface.
  @RhaiChecker::new — `pub fn` over (package_dir, config_dir, @Option @script_dir, pkg,
    config). Freezes @resolver_paths in exactly this order: `{package_dir}/scripts`,
    @config_dir, and — only when @script_dir is @Some — `{script_dir}/lib` and
    `{script_dir}/{subdir}`, subdir named by @pkg usage: @VynilPackageType::Tenant yields
    `tenant`, ::Service yields `service`, ::System yields `system`. Also scans
    `{package_dir}/scripts` exactly once, flat/non-recursive: every entry whose extension
    is exactly lowercase `rhai` joins @entry_scripts UNLESS its file NAME is in
    @ENTRY_POINT_PATTERNS (`install.rhai`, `delete.rhai`, `reconfigure.rhai`) or starts
    with `context_`. A missing scripts dir, a failed @read_dir and per-entry IO @Errs (the
    @flatten skip) all silently shrink @entry_scripts.
  @RhaiChecker::check_file — `pub fn` over (&@Path @file, &@str @source) returning
    @Vec<@LintFinding>: per-file rules plus cross-file accumulation; findings unsorted
    and undeduplicated by this file except the one name-sort noted in `Must`.
  @RhaiChecker::finalize — `pub fn` over &@self returning @Vec<@LintFinding>: the
    `rhai/unused-script` block first (iterated over the @entry_scripts @HashSet — the
    candidate ORDER is process-random), then the `rhai/unused-function` block (over
    @defined_functions — stable declaration order).
  File-private machinery (not surface, behaviour frozen below): @check_imports,
    @resolve_import, @accumulate_functions, @collect_used_vars_expr,
    @collect_used_vars_stmts, @collect_used_vars_stmt, @check_shadowing_scoped,
    @check_dead_code, @check_statements_for_dead_code, @collect_declared_vars_stmts,
    @collect_declared_vars_stmt, @check_undefined_variables, @check_empty_catch,
    @check_stmts_for_empty_catch, @extract_position, @check_unused_variables,
    @check_unused_parameters, @is_core_script, @first_property_in_dot_chain,
    @check_wrong_package_type, @check_context_hook_no_return, @check_k8s_resource_plural,
    @const @ENTRY_POINT_PATTERNS, @K8S_RESOURCE_PLURAL_KINDS, @ENTRY_POINT_FUNCTIONS,
    @FULL_ONLY_FUNCTIONS.

Accepts:
  @check_file: @file is whatever spelling the driver passes — package-root-relative (scan
    lane), the virtual `package.yaml#…` identities, or absolute — and path-text rule tests
    (substring / filename / @Path::starts_with) match those spellings verbatim; @file
    carries NO existence or readability requirement (virtual paths never touch disk).
    @source is opaque text: directive and script syntax are recognized from content alone.
  @new: any directory paths (existence beyond the guarded listing is irrelevant) and a
    @VynilPackageSource reference whose @usage is always decidable (serde default `tenant`).
  A @None @script_dir config is accepted (the two-resolver-path arm).

Returns:
  @check_file on a clean parse — findings in emission order:
    `rhai/unresolved-import`, `rhai/dead-code`, `rhai/shadowed-variable`,
    `rhai/unused-variable` (the shadowing pass runs inside the unused-variable pass and
    emits first), `rhai/unused-parameter`, `rhai/empty-catch`, `rhai/undefined-variable`,
    `rhai/wrong-api-mode`, `rhai/wrong-package-type`, `rhai/k8s-resource-plural`,
    `rhai/context-hook-no-return`; on @Engine::compile failure — exactly one
    `rhai/syntax` finding and nothing else, bookkeeping included (cascade, `Handles`).
  @finalize — `rhai/unused-script` findings, then `rhai/unused-function` findings.
  Line-number accuracy, frozen per rule: `rhai/syntax` carries the @ParseError position
    (@extract_position); `rhai/unused-parameter` carries the function body-block position
    line; `rhai/k8s-resource-plural` the kind-literal line; `rhai/wrong-package-type` the
    variable- or rhs-chain-line position verbatim (@Option, no collapse);
    `rhai/unused-variable`, `rhai/shadowed-variable` and `rhai/empty-catch` report
    position line but collapse a positionless node to @Some(0) via @unwrap_or — and 0 is
    unsuppressible because @parse_inline_disables never keys it;
    `rhai/unresolved-import` (the position IS in hand at the match and discarded),
    `rhai/dead-code`, `rhai/undefined-variable`, `rhai/wrong-api-mode`,
    `rhai/unused-script` and `rhai/unused-function` always carry @None.

Raises:
  Nothing, ever. Zero @unwrap, @expect or @panic sites in product code (verified split:
    `46` @expect fixture loads, all inside the `#[cfg(@test)]` module). The only fallible
    std calls are guarded (the single @read_dir behind @if-@Ok and its @flatten; @exists
    is boolean); option/Result values otherwise totalize through four @unwrap_or and one
    @unwrap_or_default; every @Stmt/@Expr @match destructure uses fixed-arity fields,
    never slices.

Handles:
  Parse failure — the file contributes its one `rhai/syntax` finding and ZERO
    bookkeeping: its imports never enter @imported_scripts, its entry-point definitions
    never mark its stem into @scripts_with_entry_points, its definitions/calls never enter
    the function sets. A broken file therefore cascades: a module it would have imported
    can surface `rhai/unused-script`, and a function in another file that only it (would
    have) called can surface `rhai/unused-function`.
  Import path expressions that are not string literals — skipped entirely: no resolution
    attempt, no `rhai/unresolved-import`, and no @imported_scripts entry (their real
    targets can still be reported unused).
  Names starting with `_` — exempt from the unused-variable, shadowed-variable,
    unused-parameter and undefined-variable verdicts.
  Closure definitions (rhai names starting with `anon$`) — skipped by the
    undefined-variable pass and kept out of @defined_functions, but NOT skipped by
    `rhai/unused-parameter`, so an uncalled closure parameter reports the template with a
    verbatim internal name: Parameter `v` in function `anon$1` is never used.
  Non-@System @usage — `rhai/wrong-package-type` never runs; @System packages with a path
    starting `files/` (the context-builder hook convention) are exempt too.
  Non-core script file — `rhai/wrong-api-mode` never runs; core-ness is EXACTLY filename
    `build.rhai` or `validate.rhai`, or path-string substring `handlebars/helpers/`.
  Scripts named `install.rhai`, `delete.rhai`, `reconfigure.rhai` or prefixed `context_`
    — invisible to the unused-script lane regardless of use; scripts deeper than one level
    under `{package_dir}/scripts` are equally invisible (flat scan), yet dotted import
    strings still resolve whenever the joined path exists.

Must:
  # Parsing stance (the load-bearing one)
  The engine is stock rhai — @Engine::new(), NOT any @common::rhaihandler @Script
    constructor — tuned by @set_max_expr_depths(128, 64) and
    @set_optimization_level(@OptimizationLevel::None); @Engine::compile is used solely to
    parse to @AST (or @ParseError). Everything downstream is @AST inspection: @AST::walk
    plus the hand-written recursive descents (@collect_used_vars_* collecting,
    @check_shadowing_scoped, @check_statements_for_dead_code, @check_stmts_for_empty_catch)
    — never text scoring on the source, never execution.
  @AST::walk gaps are compensated deliberately, per the source's own comments on rhai
    1.20: walk skips method-call ARGUMENTS and does not descend into try/catch bodies —
    hence the custom usage/declaration collectors and the manual nested-catch recursion.
  Runtime depth drift is structural: nesting beyond 128/64 fails @Engine::compile HERE
    while the runtime engine accepts up to 256/128 (/common/src/rhaihandler.sdd) — a
    deeply nested script receives an @Error `rhai/syntax` the runtime would never raise
    (Tasks `[?]`).
  Zero function-existence checking: no rule compares ANY called name against ANY
    registration table; unknown helper names pass lint silently and fail only at runtime —
    call-name drift is uncatchable by design (Tasks `[?]`).
  # Name tables the checker assumes (verbatim; runtime comparison per pair)
  @FULL_ONLY_FUNCTIONS, the 15 names forbidden to core scripts: `http_get`, `http_post`,
    `http_put`, `http_delete`, `http_patch`, `get_service_instance`,
    `list_service_instances`, `get_system_instance`, `list_system_instances`,
    `get_tenant_instance`, `list_tenant_instances`, `get_jukebox`, `list_jukeboxes`,
    `k8s_resource`, `k8s_raw`, `k8s_workload`.
  @K8S_RESOURCE_PLURAL_KINDS, the 8 (plural, singular) pairs: `Deployments`/`Deployment`,
    `Endpoints`/`Endpoint`, `Issuers`/`Issuer`, `Namespaces`/`Namespace`, `Nodes`/`Node`,
    `Secrets`/`Secret`, `Services`/`Service`, `TenantInstances`/`TenantInstance`; every
    other kind string is unjudged (silently accepted).
  @ENTRY_POINT_FUNCTIONS: `run`, `template`, `new`, `main` — exempt from
    `rhai/unused-function`, and their presence marks the checked file's stem into
    @scripts_with_entry_points (which exempts the matching entry script from
    `rhai/unused-script`).
  Package-type special names: the bare Variable `tenant` anywhere in the walk, and bare
    `context` accessed via Dot whose FIRST chain property (@first_property_in_dot_chain
    descends rhai's right-associative Dot/Property nesting to the leftmost) is `namespace`
    or `tenant`; `context.cluster` and every other property are clean; aliasing
    (binding `tenant` to another name) flags only the aliasing use and misses the alias.
  Runtime-name divergence, frozen (checker catalog vs /common/src registrars +
    /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd): the real registrations read `get_service_instance` plus
    `list_service_instance`, `get_system_instance` plus `list_system_instance`,
    `get_tenant_instance` plus `list_tenant_instance`, `get_jukebox` plus `list_jukebox`
    (confirmed in @crate::instanceservice, @crate::instancesystem,
    @crate::instancetenant, @crate::jukebox; the k8s mock mirror uses the same spellings) —
    SINGULAR list forms. FOUR catalog names (`list_service_instances`,
    `list_system_instances`, `list_tenant_instances`, `list_jukeboxes`) therefore match no
    registration any engine carries: real list-call sites in a core script are
    lint-INVISIBLE for `rhai/wrong-api-mode`, and a core script author using the plural
    spellings passes lint and dies at runtime with function-not-found. The http quintet
    and the k8s trio come from crates.io `vynil-core` registrars, so their spellings are
    unverifiable from this repository; `k8s_resource` is corroborated in-repo only through
    shipped /agent/scripts usage — which calls kinds far beyond the 8 pairs AND uses a
    3-argument kind-plus-namespaces form whose kind sits at position 2 and is therefore
    unchecked (Tasks `[?]`).
  Full-mode surface absent from ANY table and never checked: `s3_get_yaml` and
    `s3_list_keys` (named by /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd as the s3 registrar's script
    face), the member functions scripts get on instance objects, the file-JukeBox set that
    only the @Script::new_file_scan lane installs, the OCI names — this checker mirrors NO
    registration function of the runtime; its tables are hand-typed literals and the
    engine it compiles with is the empty stock one.
  # Rule inventory — 14 ids, levels, lanes (freeze table)
  # The seven rules that DO consult @resolve_level (`.vynil-lint.yaml` disable, override_
    and first-matching-glob can reconfigure or silence them): `rhai/syntax` (built-in
    @Error), `rhai/unresolved-import` (@Error), `rhai/undefined-variable` (@Error),
    `rhai/unused-parameter` (@Warn), `rhai/k8s-resource-plural` (@Warn),
    `rhai/unused-script` (@Warn), `rhai/unused-function` (@Warn).
  # The seven rules hardcoded-level and config-immune (settles the ./config.sdd finding):
    @Warn — `rhai/shadowed-variable`, `rhai/dead-code`, `rhai/wrong-api-mode`,
    `rhai/wrong-package-type`, `rhai/unused-variable`, `rhai/empty-catch`;
    @Error — `rhai/context-hook-no-return`.
  # Directive lanes per rule, exactly:
    FILE-UNION lane — the union of every rule id in the file's @parse_inline_disables
    ranges is what those two @resolve_level calls receive, so ONE valid directive anywhere
    suppresses the rule for the WHOLE file: `rhai/undefined-variable` and
    `rhai/unused-parameter`. NOTE: ./config.sdd's example table labels
    `rhai/undefined-variable` per-line — that label is WRONG; this file is truth.
    PER-LINE lane through @resolve_level — the finding-line set only:
    `rhai/k8s-resource-plural` (a @None-line finding feeds an EMPTY set there, making the
    directive inert for it).
    PER-LINE lane by raw map lookup, hardcoded level, outside config entirely:
    `rhai/unused-variable` and `rhai/empty-catch` (the rule id string is tested against
    @inline_disables at the declaration/catch line and reported regardless of config).
    DIRECTIVE-INERT (@resolve_level called with a fresh empty @HashSet): `rhai/syntax`,
    `rhai/unresolved-import`, `rhai/unused-script`, `rhai/unused-function` — the
    ./config.sdd inert-seam item resolves here: those four sites, and no get-at-zero site
    exists on this side.
    NO LANE AT ALL (neither config nor directive can silence):
    `rhai/shadowed-variable`, `rhai/dead-code`, `rhai/wrong-api-mode`,
    `rhai/wrong-package-type`, `rhai/context-hook-no-return`.
  # Trigger semantics (accept/reject sets)
  — `rhai/syntax` @Error: reject iff @Engine::compile @Err; every other rule runs ONLY on
    a clean parse; the position line is @ParseError @position @line (@Option).
  — `rhai/unresolved-import` @Error: @Stmt::Import whose path is @Expr::StringConstant m
    when NONE of the ordered @resolver_paths joined with `{m}.rhai` @Path::exists. The
    name m enters @imported_scripts REGARDLESS of the verdict — an unresolvable import
    still masks whatever stem it would name.
  — `rhai/dead-code` @Warn (hardcoded): at each scanned level, every statement after a
    @Stmt::Return or @Stmt::BreakLoop yields ONE identical finding each (N dead statements
    produce N repeated findings, not one per block); scanned over top-level
    @AST::statements() and manually descended Block/If/TryCatch/While/Do/For bodies;
    FUNCTION BODIES ARE NEVER SCANNED (@AST::statements() is top-level; the ignored test
    states the private-API reason); line always @None.
  — `rhai/unused-variable` @Warn (hardcoded, per-line directives): declared = every
    @Stmt::Var via @AST::walk; used = the @collect_used_vars_* traversal over top level
    AND every function body — including try/catch bodies, method-call arguments,
    assignment LHS and RHS sides, Dot/Index operands, array/map/interpolation parts,
    And/Or/Coalesce arms, and @Expr::Stmt-wrapped if/while expressions (walk is used only
    for declarations because of the gaps it has on those use shapes).
  — `rhai/shadowed-variable` @Warn (hardcoded, no lane): @check_shadowing_scoped over a
    live scope stack — top level seeds an empty frame, each function seeds a frame with
    its PARAMS; @Stmt::Block pushes one frame; @Stmt::If and @Stmt::TryCatch push one
    frame per body and per branch; @Stmt::While and @Stmt::Do one for the body; @Stmt::For
    one seeded with the loop variable. A `_`-free re-declaration of a name present in ANY
    live frame flags once, then re-inserts into the current frame (sibling scopes stay
    clean; a nested re-declaration flags exactly once).
  — `rhai/unused-parameter` @Warn (config-aware, file-union): per @iter_fn_def parameter
    (closures included) absent from the body's @collect_used_vars_stmts set; `_` prefix
    exempt; line = the @fn_def body position line (@None possible) — NOT the header line.
  — `rhai/undefined-variable` @Error (config-aware, file-union): per function definition
    whose name does not start with `anon$`, known = parameter names ∪
    @collect_declared_vars_stmts (@Stmt::Var names, for-loop variables, TryCatch catch
    bindings — the catch @Expr::Variable name); refs = @collect_used_vars_stmts over the
    body; a ref outside known and without `_` prefix is flagged, DEDUPLICATED by name and
    name-SORTED (the only order this file sorts); line @None. Closure bodies are never
    descended (the collector does not match the closure expression and `anon$` defs are
    skipped), names used ONLY inside closures therefore look unused to the
    unused-variable pass; TOP-LEVEL statements are never checked for undefined references
    at all; a top-level let REFERENCED inside a function body is NOT in that body's known
    set and flags — whether such scripts run at all depends on rhai scoping semantics at
    call time (Tasks `[?]`).
  — `rhai/empty-catch` @Warn (hardcoded, per-line directives): @Stmt::TryCatch whose
    branch block has ZERO statements; found via @AST::walk at the outer level plus manual
    recursion into nested try/catch, block, if, while/do/for bodies; a catch WITH a
    binding but no statements still flags.
  — `rhai/wrong-api-mode` @Warn (hardcoded, no lane): @is_core_script(file) (filename
    exactly `build.rhai` or `validate.rhai`, or lossy path-text CONTAINS
    `handlebars/helpers/`) AND a bare @Expr::FnCall (method calls never count) whose name
    is in @FULL_ONLY_FUNCTIONS.
  — `rhai/wrong-package-type` @Warn (hardcoded, no lane): runs ONLY for
    @VynilPackageType::System and NOT when @file @starts_with `files/`; flags the bare
    variable `tenant` (line = its position) and `context.<namespace|tenant>` first
    properties (line = the rhs-chain position, which on rhai's right-associative nesting
    anchors at the first property) — two templates, listed in `Example`.
  — `rhai/k8s-resource-plural` @Warn (config-aware, per-line): @Expr::FnCall named
    `k8s_resource` with @Expr::StringConstant at ARGUMENT POSITION 1 equal to a plural
    column member; the matching singular half is quoted as the fix.
  — `rhai/context-hook-no-return` @Error (hardcoded, no lane): applies when the file's
    lossy path text CONTAINS `context_` ANYWHERE — deliberately BROADER than @new's
    FILENAME prefix `context_` exclusion: a file like `scripts/lib/my_context_lib.rhai`
    gets the ERROR while remaining a plain unused-script candidate. The script is valid
    iff ANY function definition's LAST body statement is @Stmt::Return or @Stmt::Expr, or
    else the last TOP-LEVEL statement is (a @Stmt::Var as last statement invalidates; the
    returned value itself is unchecked); one @None-line finding.
  — `rhai/unused-script` @Warn (config-aware, directives inert): @entry_scripts member
    whose stem is neither in @imported_scripts nor in @scripts_with_entry_points; the
    finding's @file is the on-disk path anchored at @package_dir — the config glob layer
    (which ./config.sdd documents against relative paths) therefore only reaches these
    findings when the driver's directory flag was passed relative (Tasks `[?]`).
  — `rhai/unused-function` @Warn (config-aware, directives inert): every
    @defined_functions pair (all parsed-checked files collected by @accumulate_functions,
    `anon$` names dropped) whose name is in neither @called_functions nor
    @ENTRY_POINT_FUNCTIONS; membership is NAME-only across the whole package: any bare
    call or method call with the same name anywhere satisfies the identically named
    definition in ANY file, arity and receiver ignored.
  # Cross-file state invariants
  Accumulation happens ONLY on clean parses (see the cascade entry in `Handles`).
  @imported_scripts keys are raw import strings; @entry_scripts keys are stems from a flat
    disk scan — a dotted import string naming a nested module can satisfy @resolve_import
    for that module while the module itself is not even an unused-script candidate, AND
    that same string can never match a stem, so nested files rely on call-based
    suppression alone.
  Entry-point marking keys @Path::file_stem of the CHECKED @file. On the driver's virtual
    paths the filename keeps the manifest name and the annotation together, so the stem
    degenerates to the same constant string for both inline lanes: any of those inline
    texts defining one of the four entry names marks that shared pseudo-stem — an actual
    `package.rhai` script in the scripts dir would then be silenced by unrelated manifest
    content (Tasks `[?]`).
  The driver's VIRTUAL lanes still get package-side import resolution even though the
    runtime runs @value_script and @Prefly on full-API engines with an EMPTY resolver list
    (/common/src/vynilpackage.sdd): an import the linter resolves can still fail at
    operator runtime, and inline-text imports can mask real orphan scripts (Tasks `[?]`).

Must not:
  Execute, evaluate, or semantically resolve against a runtime: no registered Vynil
    function is bound, called, or name-resolved during linting, and no imported module is
    ever parsed.
  Read script content from disk, write anything, or mutate the tree — its whole disk
    surface is the @new directory listing and existence probes.
  Compute the lint verdict: blocking arithmetic belongs to the collector and the driver;
    this file only fixes levels (and for seven rules even the config cannot move those
    levels).

Example:
  Message templates (verbatim rendering; braces show the interpolation points. Where the
    note says backticked, the real message wraps that fragment in literal backticks):
    Syntax error: {e}
    Cannot resolve import "{m}"
    Unreachable code after return or break
    Variable {name} is declared but never used  — {name} backticked
    Variable {name} shadows a previous declaration — {name} backticked
    Parameter {p} in function {f} is never used — {p} and {f} backticked
    Empty catch block silently ignores errors
    Variable {name} is used but never declared — {name} backticked
    Function {name} is not available in core mode scripts — {name} backticked
    System packages cannot access tenant context
    System packages cannot access context.{prop} (not available for type:system)
    The k8s message wraps the leading call fragment in literal backticks, then continues
      outside the span; the shown form is: `k8s_resource("Secrets", ...)` uses plural
      kind; use "Secret" instead — for pair (Secrets, Secret)
    Context hook must return the context
    Script {stem} defined but never imported — {stem} backticked
    Function {name} defined but never called — {name} backticked
  Unit-test map (46 tests, 1 ignored; every suite builds the checker with
  @LintConfig::default() and @script_dir @None over the shared fixture manifest, whose
  @usage is `system`):
    syntax +/−: @rhai_syntax_error_detected, @valid_rhai_no_syntax_error
    unresolved-import −/+/exactly-1: @resolved_import_no_error,
      @unresolved_import_produces_error, @unresolved_import_no_duplicate
    dead-code: @dead_code_after_return_detected — ignored, rule has NO live test
    unused-script +/−: @unused_script_produces_warning,
      @lifecycle_hook_script_not_flagged_as_unused (lean, see Tasks)
    unused-variable −/+/RHS/LHS/underscore/try-block/dot-base/directive:
      @used_variable_no_warning, @unused_variable_produces_warning,
      @variable_used_in_assignment_rhs_no_warning,
      @variable_used_in_assignment_lhs_no_warning, @underscore_variable_ignored,
      @variable_used_in_try_block_no_warning, @variable_used_via_dot_access_no_warning,
      @inline_disable_suppresses_unused_variable
    shadowed-variable +/count-1/sibling-scope-clean/nested-flag:
      @shadowed_variable_produces_warning, @shadowed_variable_no_duplicate,
      @sibling_try_blocks_no_shadowing_warning, @nested_block_shadowing_still_warns
    unused-parameter +/underscore/method-call-arg/if-expr-init/closure(vacuous)/directive:
      @unused_parameter_produces_warning, @underscore_parameter_no_warning,
      @parameter_used_in_method_call_arg_no_warning,
      @parameter_used_in_if_expr_no_warning,
      @parameter_used_in_closure_operator_no_warning,
      @inline_disable_suppresses_unused_parameter
    unused-function +/entry-point clean: @unused_function_produces_warning,
      @run_function_not_flagged_as_unused
    wrong-api-mode +/−: @full_api_in_core_script_warns, @full_api_in_lifecycle_script_ok
    wrong-package-type + for tenant / context-namespace / context-tenant, clean cluster:
      @tenant_access_in_system_package_warns,
      @context_namespace_access_in_system_package_warns,
      @context_tenant_access_in_system_package_warns,
      @context_cluster_access_in_system_package_no_warn
    context-hook-no-return clean/error: @context_hook_with_return_ok,
      @context_hook_without_return_errors
    undefined-variable +/params/let/catch/directive:
      @undefined_variable_in_function_produces_error,
      @function_params_not_flagged_as_undefined, @let_variable_not_flagged_as_undefined,
      @catch_variable_not_flagged_as_undefined,
      @inline_disable_suppresses_undefined_variable
    empty-catch +/clean/directive: @empty_catch_warns, @non_empty_catch_no_warning,
      @inline_disable_suppresses_empty_catch
    k8s-resource-plural +/clean: @k8s_resource_plural_kind_produces_warning,
      @k8s_resource_singular_kind_no_warning
  Fixture honesty: unit tests read ONLY `package.yaml` content and the scripts-dir FILE
    NAMES of ./../../tests/fixtures/lint/rhai-checks/; the script bodies of `broken.rhai`,
    `dead.rhai`, `functions.rhai`, `params.rhai`, `variables.rhai`,
    `missing_import.rhai`, `tenant_in_system.rhai`, both `context_` files and the whole
    `handlebars/helpers/core_with_full_api.rhai` are content-dead (their NAMES or absence
    do matter to the @entry_scripts scan).

Scenario: parse failure is the only finding, and erases the file's bookkeeping
  Given source `let x = ;` → exactly the @Error `rhai/syntax` finding, message prefix
    `Syntax error: ` with the position line; the file contributes no accumulation
  Given clean source instead → no syntax finding
  Then since accumulation is clean-parse-only, a broken import file can orphan its
    would-be imported module, and a broken caller can orphan another file's function
  Mapped tests @rhai_syntax_error_detected, @valid_rhai_no_syntax_error; the cascade arm
    has none (Tasks).

Scenario: the import ladder, one finding per unresolved literal import, @None line
  Given `import "mylib" as lib;` with scripts/mylib.rhai ON DISK → silent
  Given `import "nonexistent" as x;` → EXACTLY ONE @Error with the import template and
    line @None, and the name still counts as imported
  But the @config_dir and both @script_dir resolver arms have NO test (every suite passes
    @config_dir = the fixture dir and @script_dir @None)
  Mapped tests @resolved_import_no_error, @unresolved_import_produces_error,
    @unresolved_import_no_duplicate

Scenario: finalize discharges the two cross-file rules
  Given the fixture dir scan (candidates include the orphan stem) and a check of the
    install hook defining fn run → @finalize names the orphan with the never-imported
    template @Warn
  Given a check of install_post content with fn run → `install_post` absent; NOTE the
    hook file is NOT on disk, so it never entered @entry_scripts at all and the
    @scripts_with_entry_points skip branch stays untested (Tasks)
  Given `fn helper() { 42 }` with no caller anywhere → never-called @Warn; the same
    file's `fn run(inst, ctx, args) { 42 }` clean via the entry-point table (run,
    template, new, main)
  Mapped tests @unused_script_produces_warning,
    @lifecycle_hook_script_not_flagged_as_unused, @unused_function_produces_warning,
    @run_function_not_flagged_as_unused

Scenario: variable pairs — use, shadow, and the per-line directive lane
  Given used-variable, underscore, assignment-RHS, assignment-LHS, try-block-use and
    dot-access sources → clean; a dead `let unused = 42;` → declared-never-used @Warn
  Given two same-name top-level lets → EXACTLY ONE shadowed-variable @Warn; two
    same-name lets in SIBLING try blocks clean (frames push/pop); a nested re-declare
    flags
  Given the unused-variable directive on the declaration line → that raw per-line lane
    suppresses it (no config lane exists for this rule)
  Mapped tests per the unit-test map above.

Scenario: parameters and undefined variables share the file-union directive lane
  Given `fn foo(used, unused) { used }` → the never-used-parameter @Warn at the body-block
    line; `_context` params clean; a parameter used ONLY as a method-call argument or
    inside an if-expression value stays clean
  Given that code plus the unused-parameter directive on a line → WHOLE-FILE suppression
    for that rule (the file-union lane, not per-line)
  Given a function body using the undeclared `con_bug_text` (and calling the unchecked
    helper name `log_info`) → one @Error never-declared finding at line @None; params,
    lets and the catch-bound name stay clean; one undefined-variable directive anywhere in
    the file suppresses the whole file
  Mapped tests per the map; @parameter_used_in_closure_operator_no_warning asserts a
    string the backtick template never emits — vacuous (Tasks).

Scenario: empty catch — the only hardcoded rule with a working directive lane
  Given an empty catch body → the silent-ignore @Warn at the try position
  Given a catch body with a print call → clean; the empty case with the empty-catch
    directive on that line → suppressed (per-line raw lookup, config cannot act either way)
  Mapped tests @empty_catch_warns, @non_empty_catch_no_warning,
    @inline_disable_suppresses_empty_catch

Scenario: core-mode API policy
  Given a full-API call under a `handlebars/helpers/` path → the core-mode @Warn, line
    @None, immune to config and directives; the same call in a scripts/install.rhai path
    clean
  Mapped tests @full_api_in_core_script_warns, @full_api_in_lifecycle_script_ok; the
    `build.rhai` and `validate.rhai` filename arms have none (Tasks).

Scenario: system-package context policy and context hooks
  Given fixture usage `system`: bare `tenant` access in a scripts path → the tenant-
    context @Warn at the variable line; `context.namespace` and `context.tenant` chains →
    the per-property @Warns at the chain line; `context.cluster` clean
  Given a `context_`-named path: body ending in a return of the context → clean; a
    file whose last top-level statement is a @Stmt::Var → the @Error
    context-hook-no-return at line @None; ANY function last-statement return satisfies
  Mapped tests per the map; the `files/` exemption arm has none (Tasks).

Scenario: k8s kind plural table with per-line suppression
  Given a plural Secrets call with a following chained get → the uses-plural @Warn naming
    the singular fix, at the kind literal's line; the singular spelling clean; the
    k8s-resource-plural directive on that line suppresses (the only ruleside with BOTH a
    config call and a per-line set arriving)
  Mapped tests @k8s_resource_plural_kind_produces_warning,
    @k8s_resource_singular_kind_no_warning; the remaining seven pairs, unknown kinds,
    directive behavior and @None-line inertness have none (Tasks).

Scenario: dead code inside function bodies is a documented non-behaviour
  Given code whose function returns then declares — nothing today: the scan covers
    top-level statements only, and the private-AST comment carries the reason
  Mapped test @dead_code_after_return_detected (ignored); the live top-level arm is
    itself untested (Tasks).

Scenario: config reconfiguration reaches exactly the seven resolve_level rules
  Given a manifest disable of `rhai/k8s-resource-plural` → that @Warn can vanish; an
    override of `rhai/syntax` to @Warn → the blocking verdict for broken sources can drop
  But a disable entry naming any of the seven hardcoded ids (`rhai/wrong-api-mode` among
    them) → structurally INERT; the uniformity decision sits in Tasks `[?]`).
  Mapped test: none on this checker's side (./config.sdd tests its own file, not this
    wiring).

