      `functions.rhai`, `params.rhai`, `variables.rhai`, `missing_import.rhai`,
      `tenant_in_system.rhai`, the two `context_` fixtures, and
      `handlebars/helpers/core_with_full_api.rhai` — the last one read by nothing).
  [ ] Amend ./config.sdd when next touched: its example table labels
      `rhai/undefined-variable` per-line while this file passes the FILE-UNION set, and
      the `disable` list in its own schema instance names `rhai/empty-catch` — a rule
      this checker hardcodes with no config call at all, so that entry can never act.
  [?] Name-table drift (four wrong names): the catalog list names are plural while the
      runtime registers SINGULAR (`list_service_instance` etc., confirmed across the four
      registrars and the mock mirror) — fix @FULL_ONLY_FUNCTIONS to the singular reality,
      or drop those four rather than keep a never-firing set; align docs either way.
  [?] `rhai/wrong-api-mode` semantics: the message asserts core-mode UNAVAILABILITY, yet
      every runnable lane this repository shows constructs engines carrying the full set
      (the build/validate/template/boxes/render lanes all use the full constructor; the
      file-scan lane even adds http and s3). Decide the policy: pin a genuinely minimal
      surface by constructor choice, or rewrite the message into a package-portability
      convention.
  [?] Should this checker mirror the runtime at all? It parses with the empty @Engine::new
      (zero registrations), depth 128/64 vs runtime 256/128, zero name resolution —
      authors can get lint-GREEN on names that crash at runtime, and false @Error syntax
      findings on deep nesting the runtime runs. Decide whether to build a real checked
      name+depth contract from /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd (and the core crates it
      attributes), or keep the intentionally-blind posture and document that lint never
      guarantees callability.
  [?] k8s kind posture: only position-1 string literals are judged, so the shipped
      position-2 kind argument shape is unchecked entirely, and the 8-pair table covers
      the same-file kinds only against the 20+ kinds used across /agent/scripts — sort
      kind position per arity, widen the table from a documented source of truth, or
      declare the gap intentional lint-lite.
  [?] `rhai/undefined-variable` scoping: the per-function known set ignores top-level
      declares, so a top-level variable read inside a function flags @Error HERE while
      the SAME reference silences `rhai/unused-variable` — the pair can invert exactly at
      that shape, and rhai's runtime scope-at-call decides which half is right; top-level
      statements themselves are never checked. Decide the intended scoping model for
      entry functions (they receive their data through parameters today — is that the
      contract this rule enforces?).
  [?] Closure posture: internal `anon$N` names leak into `rhai/unused-parameter`
      messages; the undefined pass SKIPS `anon$` defs while the unused collector never
      descends closure bodies, so names used only inside a closure read as unused to
      `rhai/unused-variable` (the fixture closure test happens to carry a genuinely dead
      let of its own to hide this). Normalize the three passes?
  [?] Seven config-immune rules — five of those immune to directives too, and three of
      THOSE (`rhai/wrong-api-mode`, `rhai/wrong-package-type`, `rhai/dead-code`) are the
      likeliest author-noise generators: put every rule on the @resolve_level ladder with
      per-line inline sets, normalizing the FILE-UNION lanes (one stray comment currently
      mutes a whole file) and the two raw per-line lookups that can never receive an
      override.
  [?] `rhai/unused-script` wiring: directives inert (fresh empty set reaches
      @resolve_level), iteration order process-random (@HashSet — the collector's
      insertion-order promise becomes non-deterministic here), and the finding files under
      the package-anchored on-disk path which the documented-relative glob layer cannot
      reach when the driver's directory flag was absolute. Fix wiring and freeze order.
  [?] Position-discard inventory: `rhai/unresolved-import` (position in hand, discarded),
      `rhai/dead-code`, `rhai/undefined-variable`, `rhai/wrong-api-mode` and the two
      finalize rules always report @None, while `rhai/unused-variable`,
      `rhai/shadowed-variable` and `rhai/empty-catch` report @Some(0) for positionless
      nodes — and 0 is outside @parse_inline_disables' 1-based range so no directive can
      key it. Report best-known position or @None — not 0.
  [?] Virtual-lane import contract: the driver comments declare operator-context full-API
